# Hosts that reject GitHub-hosted runners rather than being genuinely broken.
# Verified by hand: each returns 200 from a normal client but fails from CI, so
# checking them produces a weekly false-positive report instead of signal.
# Re-test before removing an entry — these are environment quirks, not permanent truths.

# Reddit serves 403 to datacenter IP ranges (200 from a residential connection).
https://www\.reddit\.com/.*

# asciinema.org times out from GitHub-hosted runners (it answers in under a second from a
# normal connection). Raising --timeout to 30 and --max-retries to 3 in check-links.yml did
# not help, so this is an environment quirk rather than a slow host. Six recording URLs were
# timing out per run, costing CI time and burying the real errors in the weekly report.
# Re-test by dropping this entry and watching one scheduled run.
https://asciinema\.org/.*

# freedesktop.org's wiki answers 418 "I'm a teapot" to GitHub-hosted runners — its anti-bot
# response, not a real status. It serves 200 to an ordinary client, and the four citations of the
# udisks page in docs/ are all valid. Not a User-Agent problem: from a normal connection it
# returns 200 both with no UA and with lychee's own, and 418 with a browser UA, so it is keying
# on address reputation rather than on the client string.
https://www\.freedesktop\.org/.*
